# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in `package.json`

### 2. SpeedInsights Component Integration
**Modified:** `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the `<Providers>` component

This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router (v13.5+), which recommends placing the SpeedInsights component in the root layout file.

### 3. Files Updated
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the latest official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (fetched on 2026-09-20). For Next.js App Router projects, the SpeedInsights component is added to the root layout file, which ensures it's available across all pages of the application.

The component was placed at the end of the body tag to avoid blocking the initial render while still capturing performance metrics for all page navigations.

## Verification

- ✅ Linter passed with no errors
- ✅ Package installed successfully (420 packages added)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful
- ⚠️ Full build requires environment variables (unrelated to Speed Insights changes)

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics. You can view these metrics in your Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section.

No additional configuration is required - the component will work automatically when deployed on Vercel's infrastructure.
